{
  "status": "answered",
  "question": "How do I parse a JSON response from an HTTP request into a Dart object?",
  "text": "To convert an http.Response into a custom Dart object, you can create a class with a factory constructor that creates the object from JSON [4][5]. For example, you can create an Album class with an Album.fromJson() factory constructor [5]:\n\n```dart\nclass Album {\n  final int userId;\n  final int id;\n  final String title;\n\n  const Album({required this.userId, required this.id, required this.title});\n\n  factory Album.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {\n    return switch (json) {\n      {'userId': int userId, 'id': int id, 'title': String title} => Album(\n        userId: userId,\n        id: id,\n        title: title,\n      ),\n      _ => throw const FormatException('Failed to load album.'),\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThen, if the server returns a 200 OK response, use the dart:convert package's jsonDecode() function to convert the response body into a JSON Map, and pass it to the fromJson() method [6]:\n\n```dart\nreturn Album.fromJson(jsonDecode(response.body) as Map<String, dynamic>);\n```",
